Description: relay notifications from local services to Telegram
 telegram-notifier is a small daemon that accepts notification requests on a
 Unix domain socket and forwards them to the Telegram Bot API.
 .
 Messages are written to a crash-safe on-disk queue before being acknowledged,
 then delivered with exponential backoff, honouring Telegram's rate limits.
 Messages that cannot be delivered are kept for inspection rather than dropped.
 .
 Recipients are configured as named targets, so different services can send to
 different chats, groups or forum topics through the same daemon. Access is
 controlled by membership of the telegram-notify group, which owns the socket.
 .
 The package also ships telegram-notify(1), a command line client suitable for
 use from shell scripts, cron jobs and systemd OnFailure= handlers.
